<title>LITHUANIA: YIELDS EDGE UP ON 91-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELDS EDGE UP ON 91-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields edged up on 91-day</p>
<p>Lithuanian government Treasury bills at Monday's auction and the</p>
<p>issue was oversubscribed, the country's central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield was 11.37 percent, up from the 10.70</p>
<p>percent offered at the last auction for 91-day paper on March 8.</p>
<p>The settlement date is March 20 and the bills mature on June</p>
<p>19.</p>
<p>All figures in millions of litas unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p>SOLD    BID     MIN/MAX YIELD   AV.YIELD   AV.LAST TIME</p>
<p>53.459  75.059  9.55/12.00	11.37	10.70</p>
<p>--Ed Stoddard, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 18</p>
